1

00:00:00,000  -->  00:00:06,420
in this exercise you're being asked to implement the structure for an agentic workflow.

2

00:00:06,420  -->  00:00:11,000
You can code agentic workflows in many ways.

3

00:00:11,000  -->  00:00:15,120
In reality, new research is coming up with

4

00:00:15,120  -->  00:00:22,440
new coding patterns to how and to implement these agentic workflows.

5

00:00:22,440  -->  00:00:27,400
There are also some new protocols that are being defined,

6

00:00:27,400  -->  00:00:31,240
such as MCP and A2A,

7

00:00:31,240  -->  00:00:37,755
which help defining what agents are and how agents communicate with each other.

8

00:00:37,755  -->  00:00:42,790
Well, we're not going to go into the details of these new protocols,

9

00:00:42,790  -->  00:00:48,790
we are going to look at a more general implementation of agentic workflows.

10

00:00:49,190  -->  00:00:56,390
In general, we will define agents as classes in Python.

11

00:00:56,390  -->  00:00:59,190
If you look at the code here,

12

00:00:59,190  -->  00:01:02,050
I have an agent class.

13

00:01:02,050  -->  00:01:08,750
Typically, this agent class will have a call to an LLM.

14

00:01:10,260  -->  00:01:17,140
In this exercise, you've been asked to enhance one of the agents.

15

00:01:18,460  -->  00:01:24,380
More specific agents are also defined as classes,

16

00:01:24,780  -->  00:01:30,380
and they may have as an input parameter an agent,

17

00:01:30,780  -->  00:01:38,980
or they might execute the code that we have in our class agent internally.

18

00:01:38,980  -->  00:01:44,780
In that case, they will receive as an input different parameters.

19

00:01:46,030  -->  00:01:49,530
Inside of the class agent,

20

00:01:49,530  -->  00:01:56,670
we define functions to execute the different capabilities of agents.

21

00:01:58,310  -->  00:02:01,810
In this case, we have a research agent,

22

00:02:01,810  -->  00:02:03,770
we have a summarizer agent,

23

00:02:03,770  -->  00:02:07,110
and we have a fact checker agent,

24

00:02:07,110  -->  00:02:09,990
which is the one that you've been asked to enhance.

25

00:02:09,990  -->  00:02:19,510
The solution to this exercise is changing the function inside of the fact checker agent.

26

00:02:20,210  -->  00:02:24,345
In this case, you've been asked to add flags.

27

00:02:24,345  -->  00:02:32,250
What we've done is we've defined flags inside of the function,

28

00:02:32,530  -->  00:02:39,275
and we're returning flags as a return from the function,

29

00:02:39,275  -->  00:02:44,450
and that adds the capability to the flag checker agent.

30

00:02:46,010  -->  00:02:52,630
If we run our demo that has all of the agents included,

31

00:02:52,630  -->  00:03:00,060
we will see that the output now has the information collected in the flags.

32

00:03:05,950  -->  00:03:09,130
After running the code,

33

00:03:09,970  -->  00:03:14,850
we can see the output from our new flags.
